WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.035
-As I mentioned before,

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.437
Alex Rodriguez
is on the show tonight!

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.272 --> 00:00:08.741
I'm so glad he's here.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.576
We actually had the chance
to work together recently.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.178
We called a baseball game
together.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.713
And it was a lot of fun.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.482
But the teleprompter operator
was kind of a loose cannon.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.518
He would put lines
into the teleprompter

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.387
that we had never seen before,
so we'd end up reading things

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.623
for the first time live on air.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.991
It was a little nerve-racking,

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.859
but I think we handled it
all right.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.161
We actually have a clip

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.963
of some of our highlights
from the broadcast.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.564
Take a look.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:38.137
♪♪

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:41.808
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.545
-Hello!
And welcome to today's game.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.113
I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:50.382
And if you're wondering,
yes, they're real.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.052
-Yes, they are.
And I'm Alex Rodriguez.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:56.288
And you can call me
little cutie.

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:58.558
Wait. Juicy Fruit booty.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:01.160
Uh, Jimmy, can I be honest?

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.995
Uh, I have an idea.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:06.666
What am I doing here?
And what baseball is?

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:10.136
Back to you, Cynthia. What?

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.304
-Well, Gonzalez
steps up to the plate.

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.540
He's hoping to raise
his batting average.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.444
But me, I'm hoping to raise
my cholesterol, which is...

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.947
why I eat one hard-boiled egg
at breakfast,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.082
one at lunch, one at dinner,

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:25.985
and one right before
making love.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.920
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.458
-You know, uh, baseball actually
reminds me a lot of making love.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.026
-Oh, yeah? Why is that?

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:37.096
-It's slow, boring.

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:40.233
And you always leave early
to beat the traffic.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.435
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:45.605
-Hey. Just a --
Just a quick reminder

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:50.209
that tomorrow night at
the stadium is Rat Night.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:52.478
Uh, the...

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.281
first 20,000 fans...
[ Laughs ]

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.616
...to arrive will get
a free, live rat.

00:01:57.616 --> 00:01:59.051
For tickets to the game,

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:02.855
call our number at 212-WET-RAT,
extension 12.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.923
[ Laughs ]

00:02:04.923 --> 00:02:06.426
Ask for Lenny Kravitz.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:09.061
No, not that Lenny Kravitz.
A different Lenny Kravitz.

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.831
Anyway, he's a good dude.
He'll hook you up with a rat.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.633
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.468
[ Applause ]

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.002
-Here's a fun fact.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:18.737
I never used to shower
after games.

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.206
-Oh.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:24.344
-I used to strip down in front
of my locker and lick myself.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:29.815
Clean my little kitty cat.
And meow, meow.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:32.518
Ish?

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.755
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.190
-You know, what makes Taylor
such a good pitcher

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.893
is that he throws
a blinding fastball,

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.396
a wicked change-up,
smelly curveball,

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:46.966
super-horny splitter,
and a boozy daiquiri.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:50.169
Oink-oink?
What does the hog say?

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.371
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.973
-I was -- I was thinking

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.209
they should make a "Space Jam"
for baseball.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.010
-Oh, yeah.
-I'll play Bugs Bunny

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:03.650
and say his famous catch phrase,
"Uh, how's it going, Docta?"

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.452
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.820
-You know,
when I root for a team,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.188
I like to say my favorite cheer.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:14.794
"Oh, mama, Dalai Lama,
Charlie Sheen, Barack Obama.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.462
Tickle me, I'll tickle you.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:20.032
Seal my butt with Elmer's Glue."

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:24.803
-I actually won the MVP
in 2003, '05, and '07.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:28.874
But he don't fool
by the rocks that I got.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:32.278
I'm still Ally from the block.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.080
Bazinga.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.015
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:43.222
♪♪

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:44.724
-We should --

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.360
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.762
We should do that more often.
-We should.

